LOCATION:Hamilton Lugar School
SUMMARY:CLACS Faculty Research Symposium with Luciana Namorato
DESCRIPTION:The Center for Latin American and Caribbean Studies (CLACS) w
 elcomes Dr. Luciana Namorato for The Other Fridas: Hidden Voices\, New Hi
 stories &amp\; Future Agendas of Latin American Women Artists\, part of t
 he Fall 2026 CLACS Faculty Research Symposium.  Thursday\, November 12th|
  1-2PM | Hamilton Lugar School GA2134  This presentation explores the rec
 ognition and representation of Latin American women artists\, considering
  how their voices and experiences can expand our understanding of the reg
 ion's artistic histories.  Dr. Namorato is an associate professor in the 
 Department of Spanish and Portuguese and co-editor of The Other Fridas: T
 he Lives and Works of Latin American Women Artists. Her research includes
  Brazilian and Portuguese literature\, gender studies\, and contemporary 
 Latin American literature.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p data-pm-slice="1 1 []">  The Center for L
 atin American and Caribbean Studies (CLACS) welcomes Dr. <strong>Luciana 
 Namorato</strong> for <strong><em>The Other Fridas: Hidden Voices\, New H
 istories &amp\; Future Agendas of Latin American Women Artists</em></stro
 ng>\, part of the Fall 2026 CLACS Faculty Research Symposium.</p><p data-
 pm-slice="1 1 []">  Thursday\, November 12th| 1-2PM | Hamilton Lugar Scho
 ol GA2134</p><p>  This presentation explores the recognition and represen
 tation of Latin American women artists\, considering how their voices and
  experiences can expand our understanding of the region's artistic histor
 ies.</p><p>  Dr. Namorato is an associate professor in the Department of 
 Spanish and Portuguese and co-editor of <em>The Other Fridas: The Lives a
 nd Works of Latin American Women Artists</em>. Her research includes Braz
 ilian and Portuguese literature\, gender studies\, and contemporary Latin
  American literature.</p><p><picture class="lw_image lw_image32516  lw_al
