 ecraft of Crisis Leadership</h4><p data-path-to-node="14">  When internat
 ional crises break\, leaders don't have the luxury of complete informatio
 n or total control. They have to make rapid strategic calls\, counter tar
 geted disinformation in real time\, and align rival organizations under i
 ntense scrutiny.</p><p data-path-to-node="15">  Skip the slides and build
  actual operational skills in <strong data-path-to-node="15" data-index-i
 n-node="55">International Crisis Response</strong>\, an interactive\, mul
 ti-agency simulation designed to test and sharpen your leadership under r
 ealistic pressure.</p><p data-path-to-node="16">  Guided by Michael Jack\
 , certified leadership coach\, international disaster strategist\, and fo
 rmer USAID Bureau for Humanitarian Assistance Division Director\, this ha
 nds-on session pushes you beyond theory into real-world strategic executi
 on.</p><h4 data-path-to-node="17">  Core Skills You'll Walk Away With</h4
 ><ul data-path-to-node="18"><li><p data-path-to-node="18\,0\,0"><strong d
