 on-Making:</strong> Practice making consequential\, high-level decisions 
 under extreme time pressure and incomplete data.    </p></li><li><p data-
 path-to-node="18\,1\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="18\,1\,0" data-index-i
 n-node="0">Crisis Communications &amp\; Disinformation Defense:</strong> 
 Learn how to deliver disciplined messaging under scrutiny\, navigate pres
 s briefings\, and actively counter viral fake news.    </p></li><li><p da
 ta-path-to-node="18\,2\,0"><strong data-path-to-node="18\,2\,0" data-inde
 x-in-node="0">Cross-Organizational Negotiation:</strong> Master coalition
 -building and gap-filling across international teams\, host governments\,
  UN bodies\, and non-profits whose interests may compete with your own.  
   </p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="18\,3\,0"><strong data-path-to-node=
 "18\,3\,0" data-index-in-node="0">Leadership Resilience &amp\; Trauma Man
 agement:</strong> Gain practical tools for managing staff decision fatigu
 e\, operational stress\, and team performance during prolonged high-press
 ure events.    </p></li></ul><h4 data-path-to-node="19">  Dynamic Rolepla
 y Structure</h4><p data-path-to-node="20">  You'll be embedded directly i
 nto key crisis response teams—representing <strong data-path-to-node="2
 0" data-index-in-node="72">U.S. Embassy officials\, UN agencies\, interna
 tional NGOs\, host government authorities\, and global media corresponden
 ts</strong>—responding live as dynamic scenario "injects" unfold.</p><h
 4 data-path-to-node="21">  ߌࠗho Can Attend?</h4><p data-path-to-node="
 22"><strong data-path-to-node="22" data-index-in-node="0">Open to all:</s
 trong> Undergrads\, Grad Students\, Faculty\, Staff\, and Community Membe
 rs. <i data-path-to-node="22" data-index-in-node="79">(Light snacks and d
 rinks provided)</i></p><h3 data-path-to-node="24">  Facilitator Bio</h3><
 p data-path-to-node="25">  Michael Jack is a certified leadership coach\,
  international crisis management strategist\, and former Division Directo
 r at USAID's Bureau for Humanitarian Assistance. He has managed disaster 
 responses across 80+ countries\, including the Iraq Sinjar crisis\, West 
 Africa Ebola outbreak\, Mexico City earthquake\, South Sudan emergency\, 
 Amazon wildfires\, and Northern Ethiopia response.</p>
